{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>You shall not take up a vain report.</b> Do not accept an oath from one who appears to you likely to transgress it, until you investigate the matter thoroughly lest he be swearing in vain. Another interpretation: do not listen to the words of one litigant lest he be speaking falsely, until his fellow litigant comes — and if perhaps he lies in his words, the other will refute him. Thus Solomon said (Proverbs 18:17): ״צדיק הראשון בריבו ובא רעהו וחקרו״. And the view of our Rabbis, of blessed memory, is that this verse is a warning against one who accepts lashon hara; thus Targum renders: לא תקבל שמע דשקר — 'Do not accept a report of falsehood.'" "<b>You shall not put your hand with the wicked.</b> The plaintiff who brings a false claim — do not assure him that you will be for him a witness of violence."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:11.329904995Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}